=begin pod :page-card<Home> :nav-order<10>

=TITLE Community

=SUBTITLE More ways of Connecting to the Raku Community

To get involved in the Raku community in general, see the main Community page at 
L<https://raku.org/community/>.  If you're keen to be involved and help, then 
your best bet is to look over the L<Troupes|../troupes> page, and find the 
troupes that best suit your skills.  

There are also some general community resources which were not significant 
enough to put on L<https://raku.org/community/> but can still be handy/helpful.  

=head1 Mailing Lists

For the folks who can't use L<#raku|https://raku.org/community/> or discord, 
there are several (low traffic) mailing lists 
I<(which use the legacy name of Perl 6)>.  

=begin table
List        | Purpose                   | Subscribe | Archive
=============================================================
perl6-users    | User questions         | L<Subscribe|mailto:perl6-users-subscribe@perl.org> | L<Archive|http://nntp.perl.org/group/perl.perl6.users/>
-------------------------------------------------------------
perl6-language | Language/specification | L<Subscribe|mailto:perl6-language-subscribe@perl.org> | L<Archive|http://nntp.perl.org/group/perl.perl6.language/>
-------------------------------------------------------------
perl6-compiler | Compiler               | L<Subscribe|mailto:perl6-compiler-subscribe@perl.org> | L<Archive|http://nntp.perl.org/group/perl.perl6.compiler/>
=end table

